<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patrice Lumumba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1925–1961</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Patrice Lumumba was a Congolese nationalist, leader of the Mouvement National Congolais, who became the first prime minister of the independent Congo in June 1960. Within weeks the army mutinied and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/katanga">Katanga</a> seceded, and his appeal for Soviet aid set him against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and President Kasavubu. He was deposed in September 1960 and killed in Katanga in January 1961 with Belgian complicity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/patrice-lumumba.jpg" alt="Patrice Lumumba" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harry Pot for Anefo ) · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PatriceLumumba1960.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
